{title: Thou Art the Way}
{artist: George W. Doane / Ralph Courteville}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: A}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Hymns Ancient and Modern, standard edition (Norwich, England: Canterbury Press, 1994), # 199)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Thou art [E]the [A]Way; to [Bm]Thee [E7]a[A]lone
[A]From [B7]sin and [F#m]death [B]we [E]flee;
[E]And [A]he who [Bm]would [A]the [D]Fa[Bm]ther [E]seek
[E]Must [A]seek Him, [Bm]Lord, [E7]by [A]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Thou art [E]the [A]Truth; Thy [Bm]Word [E7]a[A]lone
[A]True [B7]wisdom [F#m]can [B]im[E]part;
[E]Thou [A]only [Bm]canst [A]in[D]form [Bm]the [E]mind,
[E]And [A]puri[Bm]fy [E7]the [A]heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Thou art [E]the [A]Way, the [Bm]Truth, [E7]the [A]Life;
[A]Grant [B7]us that [F#m]Wa[B]y [E]to know,
[A]That Truth [Bm]to [A]keep, [D]that [Bm]Life [E]to win,
[A]Whose joys [Bm]eter[E7]nal [A]flow.
{end_of_verse}
